From 7274de01f73cbe0fd8429d485c36e7ab23461c60 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dev <dev@behemoth>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 13:20:30 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/8] RR keyswitch: single evk at P*Qmax truncated per level
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Digits = window ∩ global partition (contiguous by construction of the
inverted-terminal layout); evk rows are read positionally by global chain
index (Q part) + fixed sizeQ offset (P part). Reconstruction is purely
positional — b_j carries P*sOld only on partition-j rows, so at any level
the read rows realize P*sOld*What_{j,l}*[What_{j,l}^{-1}] for the ACTIVE
product, and raw digits need no per-level decomposition scalars. Per-level
tables are only the within-digit conversion tables (BigInteger, lazy per
level) + window-relaid P tables for ApproxModDown. EvalMultRelin drives
tensor + relin for the gate.
---
 src/pke/include/scheme/ckksrns/ckksrns-rr.h |  27 ++++
 src/pke/lib/scheme/ckksrns/ckksrns-rr.cpp   | 165 ++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 192 insertions(+)

