From 3c2e65cdc38df560b7231562ce32368193af2fb1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Davide-F5-Marincione <marincione@di.uniroma1.it>
Date: Sun, 2 Aug 2026 00:13:58 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/8] RR bootstrap setup: window-addressed CtS/StC params, RR
 drop factor, and the diagnostics that name the real blocker
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Toward RR_PLAN (c).4c step 3. Three fixes, plus the measurement that says three
fixes are not enough.

FIXED:
1. CryptoParametersRNS gains RRNumLevels / RRWindowAtLevel / RRRescaleFactorAtLevel.
   An RR level is a contiguous WINDOW of the layout and OpenFHE's level index is
   the RESCALE COUNT from the top, so level l is window nLvl-1-l. Both accessors
   THROW with the offending index and nLvl rather than reading out of bounds —
   which is what turned the next failure from a segfault into a diagnosis.
2. MakeAuxPlaintext (both overloads): the boundary-gated scale used
   GetModReduceFactor(numQ-1-level), which names a TOWER. On an RR chain no tower
   index identifies a level. Now uses F = prod(dropped)/prod(added) for that
   level's own rescale, so scFact = sf[l+1]*F/sf[l] — identically sf[l] inside a
   uniform region, differing only at the region boundary, which is the point of
   the gating. Classic and composite paths are untouched.
3. EvalCoeffsToSlotsPrecompute / EvalSlotsToCoeffsPrecompute: `towersToDrop` and
   the prefix truncation of elementParams are meaningless under RR, and
   paramsVector was built by ERASING top moduli per stage. Added an RR branch:
   stages consume one LEVEL each, and each stage's params are that level's WINDOW
   (RRStageParams), which is neither a prefix nor a truncation of one.

THE REAL BLOCKER, measured rather than assumed. With the above in, the probe
(torchfhe tests/rr_bts_setup_probe.cpp) gets past the scale and dies at
RRWindowAtLevel(43) with nLvl=27 — 43 is a LIMB count. It comes from
  uint32_t L0 = cryptoParams->GetElementParams()->GetParams().size();
and the identity that follows it everywhere:
  SetLevel(L0 - <ciphertext>.GetNumOfElements())      i.e. level = totalLimbs - currentLimbs
That identity is TRUE on a prefix chain and FALSE under RR by construction: an RR
level drops a variable number of limbs and adds others back, so limb count does
not determine level. It is not localized — 17 SetLevel(L0 - ...) sites, 8
L0 = GetParams().size() sites, 36 GetNumOfElements() uses in this file alone.

So step 3 is not three defects in the precompute, it is a pervasive level<->limb
identity threaded through OpenFHE's whole bootstrap implementation, and it needs
its own scoped pass. Recording that rather than converting sites blind: the three
fixes here are correct and needed regardless, and the accessors now make every
remaining site announce itself with an index instead of corrupting memory.

NOT installed into deps_n32 — the shipped OpenFHE is unchanged, so the classic
bootstrap is untouched. Build/test this against .rr_work/build/lib.
