Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Corrects the previous commit's handover. I suggested checking EvalAtIndexKeyGen
on the theory that rotation keys might not follow the RR single-key-at-P*Qmax
convention. They do. Verifying before building saved that work.

The guard now dumps the arrays, and they settle it:

  lvl.params[0..2] = 41680897, 36175873, 29884417   <- window, correct
  paramsD[0..2]    = 41680897, 36175873, 29884417   <- digit, correct
  evk row 0        = 41680897                        <- ROTATION KEY, CORRECT
  c[0..2]          = 36175873, 36175873, 29884417   <- ciphertext: tower 0
                                                       DUPLICATES tower 1

(My earlier reading of these moduli was wrong: I indexed them against the STOCK
chain while the probe runs the _w chain. In _w, 41680897 IS chain[0]. The key was
right all along.)

So the rotation keyswitch is correctly routed and correctly keyed; the ciphertext
handed to it is malformed. The source is the CPU ModRaise:

    temp = ctxtDCRT[i].GetElementAtIndex(0);   // take ONE tower and broadcast

which assumes the bottom modulus is a SINGLE limb. Under RR the bottom is level
0's THREE-limb ~2^78 window {tau14, tau15, q0}, so taking element 0 and
broadcasting it is the wrong operation — the audit said exactly this ("RR
ModRaise is structurally the COMPOSITESCALING shape"), and it is the CPU twin of
what RNSPoly::rrModRaise already does on the GPU (RR_PLAN (c).4c step 2). There
is no composite branch here to generalize: all 7 sites in this file are
single-limb GetElementAtIndex(0).

NOT a mechanical fix, which is why I am stopping rather than starting it. The RR
version needs the ciphertext to ARRIVE at RR level 0 (it gets there by rescaling,
which the chain's schedule does) and then CRT-extend all w limbs of that window
onto the top window. The first half is a change to the bootstrap FLOW — how many
levels ModRaise consumes and how that interacts with the level budget — not a
local edit. The CRT extension itself is already written twice (GPU rrModRaise and
compositeModRaise's shape) and is the easy half.

Still NOT installed into deps_n32.
